certbot-dns-transip (0.2.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * dns_transip.py: validate each dns_transip_domains entry looks like a
    single domain name (reject anything with internal whitespace or
    other characters a hostname label can't contain), with a clear
    error naming the ini file and the bad value. Before this, a space
    instead of a comma between two entries (a real admin mistake seen
    2026-11-04) parsed into one bogus "domain" that could never match
    any real validation_name, and ALSO excluded the whole account from
    the live-probe fallback (_find_account_and_base_domain only tries
    accounts with an empty domains list there) - so every domain for
    that account failed, with no error pointing at the actual cause.
  * tests/test_dns_transip.py: one new test for the rejection above.

 -- Personal Builder <personal@builder.invalid>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 23:10:00 +0100

certbot-dns-transip (0.2.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * dns_transip.py: create the cache/ subdirectory in directory mode if
    it does not already exist, instead of relying entirely on the
    .deb's postinst to have done so. The plugin can also be installed
    via pip (no postinst), in which case every token-cache write was
    silently failing - FileTokenCache.set() treats a missing directory
    as a plain write failure and no-ops by design, so this never
    raised an error, it just meant caching never actually worked.
    Found 2026-11-04 after a real account's dns_transip_domains value
    was accidentally space- instead of comma-separated (a separate,
    already-fixed admin mistake, not a bug here) made the symptom look
    like an intermittent caching bug.
  * tests/test_dns_transip.py: two new tests - the cache dir gets
    created when missing, and setup tolerates it already existing
    (idempotent, matches postinst's own "only if missing" behaviour).

 -- Personal Builder <personal@builder.invalid>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0100

