certbot-dns-transip (0.1.5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * dns_transip.py: support more than one TransIP account in a single
    certbot run. --dns-transip-credentials now also accepts a
    directory (containing accounts.d/*.ini, one file per account)
    instead of only a single file, for setups where domains are
    split across more than one TransIP account. Each domain is
    matched to the right
    account via an optional dns_transip_domains hint in that account's
    ini file (no API call), or failing that a live TransIP API lookup
    (unchanged single-account behaviour, now just tried per account).
    _cleanup always reuses the exact account _perform picked, never
    re-searches. Token caches move to a cache/ subdirectory per
    account in directory mode; single-file mode is unchanged.
  * debian/postinst (new): scaffolds /etc/letsencrypt/transip/{keys,
    cache,accounts.d}/ (0700, root:root) plus a disabled example
    account file and a short README, only if they don't already
    exist - never touches an admin's own files on upgrade, and never
    removes this directory on purge (it can hold real private keys).
  * README.md: document the directory/multi-account layout and the
    dns_transip_domains key - it only picks which TransIP account is
    used internally, it never affects what ends up on the
    certificate, that is still entirely controlled by -d.

 -- Personal Builder <personal@builder.invalid>  Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:50:00 +0200

certbot-dns-transip (0.1.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * dns_transip.py: build one TransipClient per certbot run instead
    of a new one for every _perform/_cleanup call, so a run - any
    number of domains - shares a single access token instead of
    repeatedly re-authenticating under the same label. This was the
    root cause of the 401 "label ... already used in another active
    access token" error, observed during a --dry-run on both
    creating and removing the TXT record. The token cache file is
    now derived automatically from the credentials INI path, no new
    config option needed. Requires transip-rest >= 0.1.2.

 -- Personal Builder <personal@builder.invalid>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:30:00 +0200

